.TH TAU 1 "2026-10-06" "tau 0.4.0" "Tau Manual"
.SH NAME
tau \- agent\-first AI CLI (non\-interactive Zig implementation of pi)
.SH DESCRIPTION
tau \- agent\-first AI CLI (non\-interactive Zig implementation of pi).
.PP
tau reads prompts from argv (with \fB@file\fR injection), calls the configured LLM provider, optionally runs tool calls in an agentic loop, and prints the result on stdout. \fB\-\-mode json\fR (the default) emits JSON/NDJSON envelopes; \fB\-\-mode text\fR emits plain text. tau is designed for AI agents and CI pipelines rather than interactive use.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtau\fR [options] [@files...] [prompt...]
.br
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-p,\fR \fB\-\-print\fR
Non\-interactive: process prompt and exit (default)
.TP
\fB\-\-provider\fR \fI<name>\fR
Provider: xiaomi (default), openai, deepseek, opencode\-go
.TP
\fB\-\-model\fR \fI<pattern>\fR
Model id, or provider/id (e.g. openai/gpt\-4o\-mini)
.TP
\fB\-\-api\-key\fR \fI<key>\fR
API key (else provider env var, else builtin)
.TP
\fB\-\-system\-prompt\fR \fI<text>\fR
Set the system prompt
.TP
\fB\-\-append\-system\-prompt\fR \fI<text>\fR
Append to the system prompt (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-mode\fR \fI<text|json>\fR
Output mode (default: json)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-stream\fR
Disable streaming (streaming is default)
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Enable streaming (overrides a no\-stream config default)
.TP
\fB\-t,\fR \fB\-\-tools\fR \fI<csv>\fR
Allowlist of tool names
.TP
\fB\-xt,\fR \fB\-\-exclude\-tools\fR \fI<csv>\fR
Denylist of tool names
.TP
\fB\-nt,\fR \fB\-\-no\-tools\fR
Disable all tools
.TP
\fB\-\-thinking\fR
Enable thinking chunks (show model reasoning)
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR
Show perf stats and tool calls (input+output)
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Report the tools that would be called; execute none
.TP
\fB\-\-temperature\fR \fI<f>\fR
Sampling temperature (default: 0.7)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-tokens\fR \fI<n>\fR
Max output tokens
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\-ms\fR \fI<n>\fR
Request timeout in ms (default: 120000)
.TP
\fB\-\-session\fR \fI<name>\fR
Persist conversation + goal to ~/.config/tau/sessions/<name>.json
.TP
\fB\-\-context\-window\fR \fI<n>\fR
Model context window in tokens (default: per\-provider)
.TP
\fB\-\-compact\-threshold\fR \fI<f>\fR
Auto\-compact above this fraction of the window (default: 0.5)
.TP
\fB\-\-compact\-keep\-recent\fR \fI<n>\fR
Tokens of recent history kept verbatim (default: 20000)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-compact\fR
Disable automatic context compaction
.TP
\fB\-\-role\fR \fI<author|critic|coordinator|none>\fR
Set the agent role (default: none)
.TP
\fB\-\-schema\fR \fI<json|@file>\fR
JSON Schema for structured output. Model must
.br
produce valid JSON matching this schema.
.br
Inline: \-\-schema '{\e"type\e":\e"object\e",...}'
.br
File:   \-\-schema @path/to/schema.json
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-iterations\fR \fI<n>\fR
Tool\-loop runaway backstop (default: 100; forces a final answer)
.TP
\fB\-\-scan\-agents\fR
Scan CWD for AGENTS.md files and list them
.TP
\fB\-\-load\-agents\-md\fR \fI<path>\fR
Load an AGENTS.md file into system context
.TP
\fB\-\-auto\-agents\-md\fR
Auto\-load cwd/AGENTS.md on startup
.TP
\fB\-\-goal\-max\-iterations\fR \fI<n>\fR
Per\-run loop cap in goal mode (default: 50)
.TP
\fB\-\-help\-json\fR
Machine\-readable help as JSON
.TP
\fB\-h,\fR \fB\-\-help\fR
Show this help
.TP
\fB\-v,\fR \fB\-\-version\fR
Show version
.SH GOAL MODE (IN THE PROMPT)
.TP
\fB/goal\fR \fI<objective>\fR
Work autonomously until the objective is audited\-complete
.TP
\fB/goal\fR \fI[\-\-tokens\fR \fIN]\fR \fI<obj>\fR
\&...with a soft output\-token budget (e.g. 250K)
.TP
\fB/goal\fR \fBstatus|pause|resume|clear|complete\fR
Manage the session's goal (needs \-\-session)
.SH ACP (AGENT CLIENT PROTOCOL) SERVER
.TP
\fBtau\fR \fBacp\fR \fBserve\fR \fI[\-\-acp\-socket\fR \fIP]\fR
Run the JSON\-RPC agent server (stdio, or a Unix socket)
.TP
\fBtau\fR \fBacp\fR \fBstart\fR
Start the ACP server as a background daemon
.TP
\fBtau\fR \fBacp\fR \fBstop\fR
Stop the background ACP daemon
.TP
\fBtau\fR \fBacp\fR \fBstatus\fR
Report ACP daemon status (JSON)
.SH AUTHOR<\->CRITIC LOOP
.TP
\fB\-\-role\fR \fI<author|critic|coordinator|none>\fR
Set the agent role (default: none)
.SH FLEET ORCHESTRATION
.TP
\fBtau\fR \fBfleet\fR \fBrun\fR \fB\-\-goal\fR \fI<text>\fR
Decompose goal into work items and dispatch workers
.TP
\fB\-\-coordinator\-model\fR \fI<model>\fR
Override coordinator LLM model
.TP
\fB\-\-worker\-model\fR \fI<model>\fR
Override worker LLM model
.TP
\fB\-\-sequential\fR
Run workers sequentially (default: parallel)
.TP
\fB\-\-items\fR \fI<json>\fR
Pre\-supplied items JSON (skip coordinator)
.TP
\fB\-\-schema\fR \fI<json|@file>\fR
JSON Schema for the coordinator response
.TP
\fBtau\fR \fBfleet\fR \fBstatus\fR \fI<id>\fR
Show fleet manifest (spec + per\-item status)
.TP
\fBtau\fR \fBfleet\fR \fBlist\fR
List active fleet ids
.TP
\fBtau\fR \fBfleet\fR \fBlogs\fR \fI<id>\fR
Show per\-worker session hint
.TP
\fBtau\fR \fBfleet\fR \fBcancel\fR \fI<id>\fR
Cancel a running fleet
.SH SKILLS (AUTODISCOVER ~/.AGENTS/SKILLS/)
.TP
\fBtau\fR \fBskills\fR \fBlist\fR
List all discoverable skills
.TP
\fBtau\fR \fBskills\fR \fBsearch\fR \fI<query>\fR
Search skills by keyword
.TP
\fBtau\fR \fBskills\fR \fBload\fR \fI<name>\fR
Load a skill into system context
.SH MODELS
.TP
\fBtau\fR \fBmodels\fR
List available providers and models
.SH GUIDE (EMBEDDED OPERATOR MANUAL \(em READ ONCE, DRIVE WITH NO EXTERNAL DOCS)
.TP
\fBtau\fR \fBguide\fR
Print the full guide as JSON (agent\-readable)
.TP
\fBtau\fR \fBguide\fR \fB\-\-human\fR
\&...as markdown
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBtau "List the files in src/"\fR
.TP
\fBtau \-\-model openai/gpt\-4o\-mini "Explain this error" @log.txt\fR
.TP
\fBtau \-\-session work1 "Remember: the build uses zig 0.16"\fR
.TP
\fBtau \-\-session work1 "/goal add a \-\-version flag and verify it builds"\fR
.TP
\fBtau \-\-session work1 "/goal status"\fR
.TP
\fBtau \-\-role author \-\-tools bash,write "add version flag"\fR
.TP
\fBtau fleet run \-\-goal "add OAuth and write tests"\fR
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBTAU_API_KEY\fR
Fallback API key, used after provider\-specific env vars.
.TP
\fBTAU_ENDPOINT\fR
Overrides the provider's endpoint URL (works for chat and tau acp). Useful for proxies, gateways, and local OpenAI\-compatible servers.
.TP
\fBXIAOMI_API_KEY, PIZIG_API_KEY\fR
API keys for the xiaomi provider (tried in that order).
.TP
\fBOPENAI_API_KEY\fR
API key for the openai provider.
.TP
\fBDEEPSEEK_API_KEY\fR
API key for the deepseek provider.
.TP
\fBOPENCODE_API_KEY\fR
API key for the opencode\-go provider.
.TP
\fBHOME\fR
Root of all tau state: ~/.config/tau/ and ~/.agents/skills/. If unset, config file, sessions, fleets, skills, and the ACP daemon are all disabled.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB~/.config/tau/config.json\fR
Optional JSON configuration file; see \fBtau\-config\fR(5).
.TP
\fB~/.config/tau/sessions/\fR
One JSON file per \fB\-\-session\fR name; conversation and goal state.
.TP
\fB~/.config/tau/fleets/\fR
Fleet manifests written by \fBtau fleet run\fR.
.TP
\fB~/.agents/skills/\fR
Skill directories autodiscovered by \fBtau skills\fR.
